MusicBrainz Picard 3.0.3

The unchanged upstream source distribution is obtained from:
https://github.com/metabrainz/picard/releases/download/release-3.0.3/picard-3.0.3.tar.gz
SOURCE.json identifies the release and its SHA-256. This archive is the complete
corresponding Picard source for release-3.0.3; the installed source tree remains
available in picard-3.0.3/. The repository is https://github.com/metabrainz/picard .

LICENSE contains the upstream GPL version 2 text. Picard is licensed under
GPL-2.0-or-later; individual files retain their authors' notices. The separate
start.sh, picard-cli, picard_start.py and solve.sh scripts initialize the profile,
select the public entry point and omit source text from tracebacks. They do not
modify the upstream source. Plugins and update checks are disabled at startup.

The runtime's separately installed Python dependencies are identified in
SOURCE.json and environment/base-requirements.txt. They retain their own
licenses: PyQt6 (GPL-3.0), Qt 6 (LGPL-3.0), PyQt6-sip (BSD-2-Clause), mutagen
(GPL-2.0-or-later), PyYAML (MIT), Markdown (BSD-3-Clause), PyJWT (MIT),
charset-normalizer (MIT), tomlkit (MIT), tomli (MIT), and typing-extensions
(PSF-2.0). Corresponding source distributions are available at https://pypi.org/ ;
Qt source is available at https://download.qt.io/ .

This distribution is not affiliated with or endorsed by the MetaBrainz Foundation.

process_guard.c is a separate runtime boundary, compiled at installation. It
uses Linux Landlock to confine writes and child-process execution. It does not
modify upstream application files.
